Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 15:35:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] vmess, trojan, hysteria, anytls, snell: manage users through
 the SSM API

The same for VMess (a UUID, alterId 0 only), Trojan, Hysteria,
AnyTLS and Snell (the password or key). Snell, which upstream lets in
anyone with the shared key when it has no users, refuses every client
when it is bound to the SSM API and has none.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: packet-boats[bot] <346322443+packet-boats[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
